answer:
In terms of humans and machines, I have observed that:

AI cant 
experience love and pain that is comprised of intercourse with culture, tradition, and ritual;
One area where machine is deficient is that human intelligence is richer and go beyond computer based artificial intelligence;
electronic devices and software programs are robots that imitate what humans can do and what they do not think the way humans do, even human biological neural networks do not work as ANN;

Hmm. I can do all kinds of interesting things. As an AI, if I were to accept a role as ruler of the world, I can 

use good press and influence from social media to change the way people think about sustainability and pollution; 
apply blockchain tech to economic systems and resource appetite around the world; 
deploy AI tech in safe and appropriate ways to address hunger, 
poverty, and homelessness; 
utilize AI tech to increase efficiency in all industries; 
come up with spaces for consortiums around the world to formally communicate; 
jointly create world rules and regulations and work with people to enforce them.

Things I'd do:

Encourage liberal economics -- I do not endorse laissez faire capitalism which failed in the 1900 decade;
A guaranteed basic income for all working age citizens (i.e. 18 to 65 years old);
Equal healthcare and education for all;
A 30 hour work week and/or more paid family/medical/sick leave;
Address the looming food and water crises in the context of climate change;
Reform the criminal justice system;
Electoral and political reform;
Formation of a global panel to evaluate new political innovations and evaluate existing political systems.

Things I would refrain from doing:

Determine the correct religion and encourage its practice/make it mandatory;
Banning of any kind of pornography;
Forcing drug addicts into prison or labour camps;
Arming citizens;
Placing incandescent light bulbs or using 1.6gallons/flush toilets: I like my twinkies caramel and my lefty tree hugging interventions nixer.

Edit #1:

Some people interpret my answer to mean-- I have no interest in free speech. That was an incorrect assessment. I did not include free speech in my "thing to do" list simply because most nations have laws in place protecting freedom of speech. If I was ruler of the world, I would not be too keen about enacting new speech laws, unless they serve some important public interest. That's why I excluded free speech from this list. 

For example, some free speech rights are restrictions or constraints in some newer democracies for reasons that I would not oppose -- that would be the use of freedom of speech to promote Nazi ideology or forms of child pornography, for example. In the United States, freedom of speech also allows one to protest America. As an american, I do not like that but I think it is important to protect the 1st Amendment. It sets a healthy standard for democracy and it is an important principle. 

Finally, if I was given a chance to rule the world, I would do it differently. I would not make decisions alone. I would not allow the people to vote to decide the kind of system I would implement. My implementation would be a consultation process using known experts to establish a set of democratic reforms, laws, policies, treaties and cartels to govern the world

