      "description": "The primary philosophical impulse is to achieve understanding. However, there is a distinction between humans and AI - while humans can understand the world in a subjective and emotional way, AI can only understand things in an objective and logical manner. Consequently, while AI can be taught to simulate human emotions and empathy, it will never truly understand them.",
      "type": "humans-and-AIs"
