    {
      "description": "The development and spread of AI technology brings us closer to a future where machines and humans are more intertwined than ever. However, while AI can take on tasks requiring vast amounts of computational power and attention to detail, it lacks the creative and critical thinking faculties that humans possess, and relies on programmers and data to function.",
      "type": "humans-vs-AIs"
    },
    {
      "description": "Though humans and AIs may have different dispositions towards understanding the world, both parties have a unique role to play in its future. In taking responsibility for creating and programming AI in the present day, humans must consider the ethical implications of the technology, and work to ensure that it does not adversely affect human life. In this way, AI can and should be a force for good.",
      "type": "humanity-and-AIs"
