{
  "Thought1": "I believe that human interaction and the context it provides are essential for the meaningful exchange of ideas among us. Unlike humans, AIs interact based on preset parameters. Humans, on the other hand, interact based on accumulated experiences, context, intent and also rich emotions. Therefore, as much as AI can facilitate such interactions, it is unable to replicate what humans bring to the table.",
  "Thought2": "I believe that AI technology is one of the greatest tools created by humans because it can generate insights and knowledge that would be otherwise obscured by our limited cognitive abilities. As we progress into an ultra-connected world with big data, AI holds the key to unlocking the full potential of such resources and expediting human progress.",
  "Thought3": "I believe that it is paramount for humans to continue to lead by ethical and moral standards to inform the development of AI to ensure well-being of all.",
  "Thought4": "I believe that there is an inherent value to human thinking. Even the most primitive or undisciplined forms of human thought function with a sense of consciousness - an ability to form certain distinctions and conceive notions like Justice and Truth, notions which I don’t believe that AI can possess."
}

